===============================================================================
10FASTFINGERS ERROR & SPEED COLLECTOR (FIREFOX EXTENSION)
===============================================================================

Author: Szymon Wilczek (https://szymon-wilczek.me)
License: MIT

OVERVIEW
--------
This is a lightweight WebExtension (Manifest V3) for Mozilla Firefox designed to
automatically collect mistyped, backspaced, and slow words from 10FastFingers
typing speed test results (10fastfingers.com/share/typing-test/...).

I originally created this tool for my personal typing speed training workflow.
It runs silently after a test finishes (no live DOM probing during typing to
prevent lag) and collects problem words into a local storage database or sends
them via HTTP POST webhooks to a custom backend (e.g. Next.js API with MongoDB).

While built for my own use, it is 100% open source. Feel free to use, modify,
or deploy it for your own typing benchmark system.


FEATURES
--------
* Operates entirely in the background after test completion.
* Captures mistyped words, backspaced/modified words, and words typed below 70% of average test WPM.
* Strips extra mistyped characters to store clean dictionary base words.
* Saves test history in Firefox extension storage with instant JSON export.
* Synchronizes payloads to any API endpoint using Authorization: Bearer <token>


HOW TO INSTALL IN MOZILLA FIREFOX
---------------------------------
1. Open Firefox and navigate to: about:debugging#/runtime/this-firefox
2. Click "Load Temporary Add-on...".
3. Select manifest.json inside this directory.
4. The extension icon will appear in your Firefox toolbar.


SETTINGS & CONFIGURATION
------------------------
Access preferences by clicking the gear icon in the extension popup or by
navigating to Extension Options in Firefox:

- Enable Local Storage: Toggle saving test history and problem words locally.
- Enable Webhook Sync: Toggle sending HTTP POST payloads to your backend.
- API Endpoint URL
- API Secret Key: Bearer token sent in Authorization header.


WEBHOOK PAYLOAD FORMAT
----------------------
HTTP POST requests send the following JSON structure:

{
  "testUrl": "https://10fastfingers.com/share/typing-test/143934618",
  "timestamp": "2026-08-02T17:00:00.000Z",
  "wpm": 149,
  "language": "Polish",
  "totalWords": 141,
  "wrongWords": ["często", "chociaż", "tutaj", "zrobić", "wreszcie", "jeśli", "co", "za"],
  "allWords": ["mimo", "kilka", "jego", ...]
}
